Terma 1.8.1
Copyright: zmide and the Terma contributors; see upstream source notices.
License: GPL-3.0-only
Upstream: https://github.com/zmide/Terma
Source revision: 1a86e73241547d92b5822320bf1eb14f8885503e
Source: https://github.com/zmide/Terma/tree/1a86e73241547d92b5822320bf1eb14f8885503e

This package redistributes the compiled Web application and browser assets from
the official Terma 1.8.1 source release. Its original archive, containing the
application source, compiled output, dependency lock, and build scripts, is
included in the distribution bundle as terma.source-Terma-1.8.1-linux-source-noarch.tar.gz.
The recipe retains upstream application behavior and applies upstream's
patch-ssh2-sftp-raw.js and prepare-zmodem-runtime.js to the locked dependencies.
It supplies a foreground launcher and systemd service for ZimaOS. It does not
redistribute Electron, VcXsrv, TigerVNC Viewer, or fnOS integration.

The private runtime is the official Node.js 22.23.5 Linux distribution:
https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.5/
Node.js source: https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.5/node-v22.23.5.tar.xz
Its LICENSE includes the Node.js MIT license and bundled component notices.
The verified runtime archive is included in terma.runtime-sources.tar.

Production npm versions and SHA-512 integrity values come from the upstream
release's package-lock.json. Registry URLs are normalized to registry.npmjs.org
without changing versions or integrity values. Dependency install scripts are
disabled. node-pty and @serialport/bindings-cpp are built from those sources on
matching Linux hardware, using the pinned Node.js headers and bundled node-gyp.
SSH2 uses its JavaScript cryptographic fallback without its optional accelerator.
Foreign-platform prebuilds and intermediate native build files are omitted.

terma.runtime-packages.json records every installed npm component's lock path,
version, source URL, and SHA-512. terma.runtime-sources.tar includes their
unmodified verified npm tarballs, named by SHA-512. This includes noVNC's
MPL-2.0 source and the original sources used by the upstream ZMODEM and SSH2
preparation scripts. The Terma source archive supplies those scripts.

License texts are installed under /usr/share/licenses/terma/: LICENSE for Terma,
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for upstream's component overview, Node.js-LICENSE for
the private runtime, NotoSansSC-OFL.txt for the bundled font, and third-party/
for dependency license and notice files. The upstream overview covers desktop
components that are not included in this Web package. Individual components
retain their own licenses, including MIT, BSD, ISC, Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0, and
SIL-OFL-1.1. Source URLs and inventories supplement these license texts.

Package integration code uses this repository's MIT license, installed as
/usr/share/licenses/terma/packaging/LICENSE. The README documents service
privileges, persistent data, updates, and removal.
